# XSH atomic_flag_test_and_set(), atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# ATOMIC_FLAG_INIT (<stdatomic.h>) is used to make flags that start clear.

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_test_and_set.001
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/stdatomic.h.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A flag initialized with ATOMIC_FLAG_INIT (automatic, static, a
           structure member, array elements) is clear: the first
           atomic_flag_test_and_set() returns false and sets it, and every
           later call returns true.
test       t/001-test-and-set.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_test_and_set.002
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit() with each of the six memory
           orders returns false for a clear flag (setting it) and true
           afterwards; the plain form then also returns true.
test       t/002-explicit-orders.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_test_and_set.003
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.15.1
class      required
since      2024
says       A spin lock taking a flag with atomic_flag_test_and_set() (acquire
           or default order) and releasing it with atomic_flag_clear()
           (release or default order) excludes: four threads incrementing an
           ordinary counter 5000 times each under it never overlap and the
           counter ends at 20000.
note       A thread that cannot take the lock within 30 s makes the test
           UNRESOLVED (a flag that never sets, or one that is never
           cleared, is judged by XSH.atomic_flag_test_and_set.001 and
           XSH.atomic_flag_clear.001).
test       t/003-spinlock.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_flag_test_and_set.004
anchor     functions/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.15.1
class      required
since      2024
says       Four threads calling atomic_flag_test_and_set() on a clear flag at
           the same time, over 1024 rounds with a fresh flag each, never
           see false more than once nor fewer: exactly one thread sees the
           flag clear in each round.
test       t/004-single-winner.c
